      "unit": "u12",
      "source": "5 Maintenance\nMaintain the pump with care. Read the instructions carefully and pay special attention to the warnings!\nAlways have spare shaft seals and rubber seals to hand.\nSee separate motor instructions.\nCheck the pump for smooth operation after service.\nRRRuuubbbbbbeeerrr ssseeeaaalllsss\nSSShhhaaafffttt ssseeeaaalll\nMotor bearings\nRRReeeppplllaaaccceee aaafffttteeerrr 111222 mmmooonnnttthhhsss:::\nPreventive maintenance\nReplace when replacing the\n(one-shift) complete shaft seal shaft seal\nRRReeeppplllaaaccceee aaattt ttthhheee eeennnddd ooofff ttthhheee Replace when replacing the\nMaintenance after leakage\n(leakage normally starts slowly) dddaaayyy::: complete shaft seal\nshaft seal\nPlanned maintenance\n- Regular inspection for\nReplace when replacing the Yearly inspection is\nleakage and smooth\nshaft seal\nrecommended\noperation\n- Replace complete bearing\n- Keep a record of the pump\nif worn\n- Use the statistics for\n- Ensure that the bearing is\ninspection planning\naxially locked (see motor\ninstructions)\nRRReeeppplllaaaccceee aaafffttteeerrr llleeeaaakkkaaagggeee:::\nComplete shaft seal\nBBBeeefffooorrreee fffiiittttttiiinnnggg\nBBBeeefffooorrreee fffiiittttttiiinnnggg\nLubrication\nLubricate the O-rings with\nSilicone grease or silicone oil\nsilicone grease or silicone oil\nPPPrrreee---uuussseee ccchhheeeccckkk\nCCCAAAUUUTTTIIIOOONNN!!!\nFit the electrical connections correctly if they have been removed from the motor during servicing.\n(See pre-use check in section 3.1 Unpacking/delivery).\nPPPaaayyy ssspppeeeccciiiaaalll aaatttttteeennntttiiiooonnn tttooo wwwaaarrrnnniiinnngggsss!!!",
